<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/capabilityOf> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/dispositionOf> ;
                                                            owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasCapability> ;
                                                            rdfs:label "capabilityOf" ;
                                                            rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasCapability> ;
                                                            <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                            <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'has capability'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/concretizedBy
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/concretizedBy> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                             owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/concretizes> ;
                                                             rdfs:label "concretizedBy" ;
                                                             rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/concretizes> ;
                                                             <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                             <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'concretizes'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/concretizes
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/concretizes> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                           rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                         owl:unionOf ( <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Activity>
                                                                                       <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/PhysicalObject>
                                                                                     )
                                                                       ] ;
                                                           rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/InformationObject> ;
                                                           rdfs:label "concretizes" ;
                                                           rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000059> ,
                                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000164> ,
                                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000059> ,
                                                                        <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/concretizedBy> ;
                                                           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A report is produced as paper copies, a spreadsheet document is shown on a computer screen, a plan is carried out, a device operates according to a functional specification, a software program is executed." ;
                                                           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Inspired by BFO's \"concretizes\". The constraints on 'concretizes' in IDO closely matches that employed in BFO-ISO (obo:BFO_0000059), and not the RO or the IAO (obo:RO_0000059)." ;
                                                           <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                           <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'concretizes' y, then y is an 'information object', and x is a 'physical object' copy of y, or an 'activity' performance of y." ;
                                                           <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "A comprehensive definition of what it means to be a copy, or manifest a pattern, is beyond the scope of IDO. The definition given here is clearly incomplete." ;
                                                           <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "The relation of concretization is under-documented, especially when it comes to concretization as entities to be realized in activities, or activities themselves; we follow the latter, as is done in BFO-ISO, where the performance of a musical piece is the concretization. Other BFO documentation says the intention to perform is the concretization.  The current annotations and axioms in IDO represent a best effort, but may need to be changed." ,
                                                                                                                                                     "There are two main, and very different, uses of 'concretizes' for an information object y.  (1) The information object is made concrete in printed or electronic copies. Each copy will have patterns of ink or configurations of electrons that map to y: a quality of appropriate similarity.  (2) The information object is made concrete by a performance according to the specification given by y. A 'process profile' of the performance will map to the pattern of y in an appropriate way." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/concretizes> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000059> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000059 is 'concretizes at some time', from BFO-ISO"
 ] .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/concretizes> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000164> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000164 is 'concretizes at all times', from BFO-ISO"
 ] .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/concretizes> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000059> ;
   rdfs:comment "RO_0000059 is 'concretizes', from the Relations Ontology; also used in the Information Artifact Ontology."
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/connectedTo
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/connectedTo> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ,
                                                                    owl:SymmetricProperty ;
                                                           rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/PhysicalObject> ;
                                                           rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/PhysicalObject> ;
                                                           rdfs:label "connectedTo" ;
                                                           rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002170> ,
                                                                        "ISO 15926-2:2003 'connection_of_individual'" ;
                                                           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A three-pin electrical plug is connected to a three-pin socket, two flanges are connected with bolts and a gasket, a gas compressor is indirectly connected to a gearbox assembly (via a coupling)." ;
                                                           <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                           <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x is 'connected to' y, then there is a physical connection between x and y." ;
                                                           <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "The notion of being connected to is primitive; an account would require an account of connection activities and constancy of material objects between the connected individuals." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/connectedTo> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002170> ;
   rdfs:comment "RO_0002170 is 'connected to', in the Relations Ontology."
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/containedBy
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/containedBy> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                           rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/locatedRelativeTo> ;
                                                           owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/contains> ;
                                                           rdfs:label "containedBy" ;
                                                           rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/contains> ;
                                                           <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                           <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'contains'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/contains
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/contains> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                        rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/locatedRelativeTo> ;
                                                        rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/PhysicalObject> ;
                                                        rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/PhysicalObject> ;
                                                        rdfs:label "contains" ;
                                                        rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000124> ,
                                                                     <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001015> ,
                                                                     <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/containedBy> ,
                                                                     "ISO 15926-2:2003 'containment_of_individual'" ;
                                                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "An instrument is contained in an enclosure, an pump contains an impeller, a device is contained by a volume of inert gas, a pipeline inspection gauge (pig) is located inside a pipeline." ;
                                                        <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                        <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'contains' y, then x and y are 'physical object's, and y is located entirely within x." ;
                                                        <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "The notion of being \"located within\" is not fully defined here, leaving open whether this is understood in terms of boundaries of physical objects or a fixed frame of reference." ;
                                                        <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "This relation is intended to be used where an object x is located inside another object y, but x not is not a part of y (as would be the case, e.g., for an assembly)." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/contains> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000124> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000124 is 'location of at some time' in BFO-ISO."
 ] .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/contains> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0001015> ;
   rdfs:comment "RO_0001015 is 'location of' in the Relations Ontology."
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/contentPartOf
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/contentPartOf> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                             rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/partOf> ;
                                                             owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasContentPart> ;
                                                             rdfs:label "contentPartOf" ;
                                                             rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasContentPart> ;
                                                             <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                             <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'has content part'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/createdBy
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/createdBy> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/passiveParticipantIn> ;
                                                         owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/creates> ;
                                                         rdfs:label "createdBy" ;
                                                         rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/creates> ;
                                                         <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                         <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'creates'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/creates
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/creates> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                       rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPassiveParticipant> ;
                                                       rdfs:comment "Use this relation to express that an activity brings an object into being." ;
                                                       rdfs:label "creates" ;
                                                       rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/createdBy> ,
                                                                    "ISO 15926-2:2003 'class_of_cause_of_beginning_of_class_of_individual'" ;
                                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A manufacturing activity produces a car, a welding activity produces a piping spool, a measurement activity produces a performance log." ;
                                                       <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                       <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "if x 'creates' y, then x is an 'activity', y is an 'object', and x brings y into being." ;
                                                       <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "A comprehensive definition of the notion of creation is beyond the scope of IDO." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/creates> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget "ISO 15926-2:2003 'class_of_cause_of_beginning_of_class_of_individual'" ;
   rdfs:comment "ISO 15926-2:2003, p. 132 provides an example as, \"A car manufacturing activity causes the beginning of a car\"."
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/datumUOM
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/datumUOM> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                        rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasContentPart> ;
                                                        owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/uomOfDatum> ;
                                                        rdf:type owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                                                        rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/QualityDatum> ;
                                                        rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/UnitOfMeasure> ;
                                                        rdfs:label "datumUOM" ;
                                                        rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000039> ,
                                                                     <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002536> ,
                                                                     <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unit> ,
                                                                     <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/uomOfDatum> ,
                                                                     <http://www.ontology-of-units-of-measure.org/resource/om-2/hasUnit> ,
                                                                     "https://schema.org/unitCode" ;
                                                        <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The measured datum \"55 degrees Celsius\" has Celsius as unit of measure." ;
                                                        <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                        <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has datum uom' y, then x is a 'quality datum' for which any 'datum value' is interpreted by the 'unit of measure' y." ;
                                                        <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "Interpretation in terms of a unit is not defined." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/datumUOM> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000039> ;
   rdfs:comment "IAO_0000039 is 'has measurement unit label' in the Information Artifact Ontology."
 ] .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/datumUOM> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0002536> ;
   rdfs:comment "RO_0002536 is 'measurement property has unit', an annotation property in the Relations Ontology."
 ] .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/datumUOM> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget "https://schema.org/unitCode" ;
   rdfs:comment "unitCode is a property in the Schema.org vocabulary."
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/directlyConnectedTo
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/directlyConnectedTo> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                   rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/connectedTo> ;
                                                                   rdf:type owl:SymmetricProperty ;
                                                                   rdfs:label "directlyConnectedTo" ;
                                                                   rdfs:seeAlso "ISO 15926-2:2003 'direct_connection'" ;
                                                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "An electrical plug is connected to a socket, a tag plate is welded to a pressure vessel." ;
                                                                   <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                   <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x is 'directly connected to' y, then x is 'connected to' y, and any material present between x and y directly serves to maintain the connection." ;
                                                                   <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "The notion of maintaining connection is not defined; what counts as a direct connection is hard to define precisely." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/dispositionOf
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/dispositionOf> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                             rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/potentialOf> ;
                                                             owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasDisposition> ;
                                                             rdfs:label "dispositionOf" ;
                                                             rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasDisposition> ;
                                                             <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                             <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'has disposition'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/ends
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/ends> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                    rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/activityBoundOf> ;
                                                    owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasEnding> ;
                                                    rdfs:label "ends" ;
                                                    rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasEnding> ;
                                                    <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                    <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'has ending'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/featureOf
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/featureOf> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/arrangedPartOf> ;
                                                         owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasFeature> ;
                                                         rdfs:label "featureOf" ;
                                                         rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasFeature> ;
                                                         <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                         <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'has feature'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/functionOf
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/functionOf> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                          rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/capabilityOf> ;
                                                          owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasFunction> ;
                                                          rdfs:label "functionOf" ;
                                                          rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasFunction> ;
                                                          <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                          <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'has function'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/functionalPartOf
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/functionalPartOf> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/partOf> ;
                                                                owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasFunctionalPart> ;
                                                                rdfs:label "functionalPartOf" ;
                                                                rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasFunctionalPart> ;
                                                                <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'has functional part'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasActiveParticipant
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasActiveParticipant> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                    rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasParticipant> ;
                                                                    rdfs:label "hasActiveParticipant" ;
                                                                    rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/activeParticipantIn> ;
                                                                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A hammer is the tool in a nail-driving activity, a pressure transmitter outputs data in a monitoring activity, a maintenance engineer replaces an instrument in a repair activity, a light sensor controls the level of illumination." ;
                                                                    <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                    <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has active participant' y, then x is an active participant in y." ;
                                                                    <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "The distinction between active and participation participation is primitive." ;
                                                                    <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "This is a covering relation for participation that involves acting on other participants." ,
                                                                                                                                                              "With OWL property chains, the right kind of participation can be secured for activities that count as realizations of 'potential' individuals. As in, a pump's primary function is realized in pumping activities, but only provided the pump is actually doing the pumping, acting as an \"agent\" or \"subject\"." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasActivityBound
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasActivityBound> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasActivityPart> ;
                                                                rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Event> ;
                                                                rdfs:label "hasActivityBound" ;
                                                                rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/activityBoundOf> ,
                                                                             "ISO 15926-2:2003 'temporal_bounding'" ;
                                                                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The moment an electrical connection is broken, the time that a fluid reaches a set temperature." ;
                                                                <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has activity bound' y, then x 'has activity part' y, and y is an 'event'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasActivityPart
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasActivityPart> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                               rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasTemporalPart> ;
                                                               rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Activity> ;
                                                               rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Activity> ;
                                                               rdfs:label "hasActivityPart" ;
                                                               rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000117> ,
                                                                            <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/activityPartOf> ,
                                                                            "ISO 15926-2:2003 'temporal_whole_part'" ;
                                                               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The startup period of a chemical process, the inspection part of a maintenance activity, the moment a software program terminates execution." ;
                                                               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "Parts of activities may be determined by a range of criteria, including temporal restrictions (to sub-periods), spatial restrictions (parts that occupy sub-volumes of space), by the engagement of participants (temporal or spatial parts where one or more participants are active), and \"selective abstraction\" to profiles (parts determined by that which affects variation in selected qualities)." ;
                                                               <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                               <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has activity part' y, then x and y are activities, and x 'has arranged part' y." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasActivityPart> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000117> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000117 is 'has occurrent part' in BFO-ISO. This relation has 'occurrent' as domain and range, where the IDO 'has activity part' is restricted to just 'activity'."
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasActivityProfile
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasActivityProfile> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                  rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasActivityPart> ;
                                                                  rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/ActivityProfile> ;
                                                                  rdfs:comment "BFO_0000133 is 'process profile of', in the Molecular Process Ontology and other BFO-based ontologies." ;
                                                                  rdfs:label "hasActivityProfile" ;
                                                                  rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000133> ,
                                                                               <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/activityProfileOf> ;
                                                                  <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A pipeline transport activity has a \"profile\" part which is the variation in fluid pressure." ;
                                                                  <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                  <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has activity profile' y, then x 'has activity part' y, and y is determined by selective abstraction to that part of x that effects variation in some quality of a participant in x." ;
                                                                  <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "The notion of selective abstraction is not defined." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasArrangedPart
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasArrangedPart> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                               rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPart> ;
                                                               rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/PhysicalObject> ;
                                                               rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/PhysicalObject> ;
                                                               rdfs:label "hasArrangedPart" ;
                                                               rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000024> ,
                                                                            <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/arrangedPartOf> ,
                                                                            "ISO 15926-2:2003 'arrangement_of_individual'" ;
                                                               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The upper half of a pressure vessel, the mid-section of a bridge. The buildings on a campus, arranged as parts." ;
                                                               <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                               <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has arranged part' y, then y is a part of x with a boundary determined in relation to other parts of x." ;
                                                               <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "The notion of determinate boundary is taken as primitive. For further details, refer to the explanation  of \"fiat part\" in the BFO documentation." ;
                                                               <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "The parts do not have to be connected to each other.  They may be separable or non-separable." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasArrangedPart> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000024> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000024 is 'fiat object part' in BFO-ISO."
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasAssembledPart
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasAssembledPart> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasArrangedPart> ;
                                                                rdfs:label "hasAssembledPart" ;
                                                                rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/assembledPartOf> ,
                                                                             "ISO 15926-2:2003 'assembly_of_individual'" ;
                                                                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A pipe bend welded into a piping spool, the protective sheath on an electrical cable, a door-handle in a door, a storey of a building." ;
                                                                <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has assembled part' y, then y is a connected 'arranged part' of x." ;
                                                                <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "The notion of connection is primitive." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasBeginning
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasBeginning> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                            rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasActivityBound> ,
                                                                               <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasBeginning> ;
                                                            rdfs:label "hasBeginning" ;
                                                            rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000222> ,
                                                                         <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/begins> ,
                                                                         "ISO 15926-2:2003 'beginning'" ;
                                                            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The event that light is switched on, the start of filling a tank." ;
                                                            <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                            <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has beginning' y, then y is an 'event' which 'has temporal extent' some 'instant' which is the first instant of the temporal extent of x." ;
                                                            <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "The notion of first instant is not defined." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasBeginning> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000222> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000222 is 'has first instant' in BFO-ISO, defined for 'temporal region' (differently from 'has beginning' in IDO, defined for 'activity')."
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasCapability
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasCapability> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                             rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasDisposition> ;
                                                             rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Capability> ;
                                                             rdfs:comment "Inspired by the introduction of the class 'capability' in recent works by Barry Smith, this relation complements 'has disposition' and 'has function'." ;
                                                             rdfs:label "hasCapability" ;
                                                             rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/capabilityOf> ;
                                                             <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A pressure sensor has the capability of being a level sensor, a wall has the capability of noise insulation." ;
                                                             <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                             <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "x 'has capability' y if and only if x 'has potential' y, and y is a 'capability'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasContentPart
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasContentPart> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                              rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPart> ;
                                                              rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/InformationObject> ;
                                                              rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/InformationObject> ;
                                                              rdfs:comment "Introduced February 2024 as superproperty for parts of information objects." ;
                                                              rdfs:label "hasContentPart" ;
                                                              rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/contentPartOf> ;
                                                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A part of a document such as a chapter, section or figure" ;
                                                              <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                              <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has content part' y, then x and y are information objects, and x 'has part' y." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasDisposition
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasDisposition> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                              rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPotential> ;
                                                              rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Disposition> ;
                                                              rdfs:label "hasDisposition" ;
                                                              rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000197> ,
                                                                           <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000091> ,
                                                                           <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/dispositionOf> ;
                                                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A bolted joint has a disposition to come loose, a motor has a disposition to vibrate, a steel bar has a disposition to rust, a vessel has a disposition to leak, a volatile gas has a disposition to flow upwards." ;
                                                              <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                              <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "x 'has disposition' y if and only if x 'has potential' y, and y is a 'disposition'." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasDisposition> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000197> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000197 is 'inheres in'"
 ] .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasDisposition> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000091> ;
   rdfs:comment "RO_0000091 is 'has disposition'"
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasEnding
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasEnding> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasActivityBound> ,
                                                                            <http://www.w3.org/2006/time#hasEnd> ;
                                                         rdfs:label "hasEnding" ;
                                                         rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000224> ,
                                                                      <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/ends> ,
                                                                      "ISO 15926-2:2003 'ending'" ;
                                                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The event that light is switched off, the end of filling a tank." ;
                                                         <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                         <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has ending' y, then y is an 'event' which 'has temporal extent' some 'instant' which is the last instant of the temporal extent of x." ;
                                                         <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "The notion of last instant is not defined." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasEnding> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000224> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000224 is 'has last instant' in BFO-ISO, defined for 'temporal region' (differently from 'has ending' in IDO, defined for 'activity')."
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasFeature
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasFeature> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                          rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasArrangedPart> ;
                                                          rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Feature> ;
                                                          rdfs:label "hasFeature" ;
                                                          rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/featureOf> ,
                                                                       "ISO 15926-2:2003 'feature_whole_part'" ;
                                                          <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A flange face, a corrosion protected surface, the contact surface of an electrical plug." ;
                                                          <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                          <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has feature' y, then y is a non-separable, contiguous 'arranged part' of x." ;
                                                          <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "The notion of non-separable and contiguous part is primitive." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasFeature> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget "ISO 15926-2:2003 'feature_whole_part'" ;
   rdfs:comment "The definition is lifted directly from 'feature whole part' of ISO 15926-2:2003."
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasFunction
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasFunction> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                           rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasCapability> ;
                                                           rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Function> ;
                                                           rdfs:label "hasFunction" ;
                                                           rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000197> ,
                                                                        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000085> ,
                                                                        <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/functionOf> ,
                                                                        "ISO 15926-2:2003 'functional_physical_object'" ;
                                                           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A pump has the function of moving fluids, a door has the function of an explosion barrier." ;
                                                           <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                           <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "x 'has function' y if and only if x 'has potential' y, and y is a 'function'." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasFunction> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000085> ;
   rdfs:comment "RO_0000085 is 'has function'"
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasFunctionalPart
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasFunctionalPart> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                 rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPart> ;
                                                                 rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/System> ;
                                                                 rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/FunctionalObject> ;
                                                                 rdfs:label "hasFunctionalPart" ;
                                                                 rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/partOf> ;
                                                                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A separation system has a cooling system as functional part." ;
                                                                 <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                 <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has functional part' y, then x is a 'system' of which y is a part, and y has one or more functions that contribute to the function of x." ;
                                                                 <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "The notion of \"contributing function\" is not fully accounted for in IDO." ;
                                                                 <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "'has functional part' is used to represent the functional break-down of a system. Where x is a functional part of a system y, the realisation of one or more functions of x contributes to the performance of y." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasInterest
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasInterest> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                           rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPotential> ;
                                                           owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/interestOf> ;
                                                           rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                         owl:unionOf ( <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Organism>
                                                                                       <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Organization>
                                                                                     )
                                                                       ] ;
                                                           rdfs:comment "Note, the use of \"potential\" in the definition does not imply \"not actual\", only \"not necessarily actual\"." ;
                                                           rdfs:label "hasInterest" ;
                                                           rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000033> ,
                                                                        <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/interestOf> ,
                                                                        "ISO 15926-2:2003 'lifecycle_stage'" ;
                                                           <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "An intention to start a process, a plan to modify a plant, an approval of a certification." ;
                                                           <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/explanatoryNote> "The relation of interest receives a related, but different treatment in Merrell, et al., \"Capabilities\" (cf. annotations on 'capability'), p. 14: \"We take the 'has an interest in' relation to be primitive, ... [T]he domain of this relation is: all organisms and groups of organisms, ... [T]he range is process in BFO terms, specifically all processes that are the realizations of dispositions.\" With IDO, the range is instead a 'potential'; this allows for interests that are not realized." ;
                                                           <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                           <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "x 'has interest' y if and only if x is an 'organization' or 'organism', x 'has potential' y, and y is an 'interest'." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasInterest> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000033> ;
   rdfs:comment "IAO_0000033 is 'directive information entity' in the Information Artifact Ontology. See, e.g., subtypes 'action specification', 'objective specification', 'plan specification'; and specifically, 'software' as a subtype of 'plan specification'."
 ] .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasInterest> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget "ISO 15926-2:2003 'lifecycle_stage'" ;
   rdfs:comment "Derived from the relation 'lifecycle_stage' of ISO 15926-2:2003, which has the attribute pair 'interest'/'interested'; 'class_of_lifecycle_stage' provides examples of specialisations as, \"EXAMPLE Planned, required, expected, and proposed can be represented by instances of [class_of_lifecycle_stage].\" Following this, 'interest of' is a superproperty suitable for various intentional relationships, such as planning, approving, or ordering. With IDO, we restrict interest to 'potential' entities, while in ISO 15926-2:2003 the domain and range are both unrestricted."
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasMaterialPart
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasMaterialPart> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                               rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPart> ;
                                                               owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/materialPartOf> ;
                                                               rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/PhysicalObject> ;
                                                               rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Compound> ;
                                                               rdfs:label "hasMaterialPart" ;
                                                               rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/materialPartOf> ;
                                                               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A laptop cover has aluminium and plastic material parts." ;
                                                               <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                               <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has material part' y, then x is a 'physical object', and y is a maximal part of x that has a certain 'material composition quality'." ;
                                                               <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "The reference in the definition to some 'material composition quality' possessed by the part can not be captured in OWL." ;
                                                               <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "This is a hook for sub-properties to assist with representation of concepts associated with, e.g., recyclability." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPart
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPart> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                       owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/partOf> ;
                                                       rdfs:label "hasPart" ;
                                                       rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051> ,
                                                                    <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000117> ,
                                                                    <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000178> ,
                                                                    <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/partOf> ,
                                                                    <http://www.loa-cnr.it/ontologies/DOLCE-Lite.owl#part> ,
                                                                    <http://www.w3.org/ns/ssn/hasSubSystem> ,
                                                                    "ISO 15926-2:2003 'composition_of_individual'" ;
                                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A system has functional parts, a process has stages, a plant is partitioned into areas." ;
                                                       <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                       <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has part' y, then y is a part of x." ;
                                                       <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "Parthood is a primitive for ontologies." ;
                                                       <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "The relationship x 'has part' y implies that y  is physically or conceptually associated with x, contributing to its  structure, functionality, or characteristics." ,
                                                                                                                                                 "Where possible, the sub-properties should be used. This property can be used for arbitrary aggregates." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPart> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000051> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000051 is 'has part', in the Information Artefact Ontology and in the Relations Ontology (in the latter, BFO_0000051 appears as a subrelation of 'overlaps')."
 ] .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPart> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000117> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000117 is 'has occurrent part' in BFO-ISO."
 ] .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPart> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000178> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000178 is 'has continuant part of at some time' in BFO-ISO."
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasParticipant
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasParticipant> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                              owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/participantIn> ;
                                                              rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Activity> ;
                                                              rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Object> ;
                                                              owl:propertyChainAxiom ( <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasActivityPart>
                                                                                       <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasParticipant>
                                                                                     ) ,
                                                                                     ( <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/profileOfQuality>
                                                                                       <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/qualityOf>
                                                                                     ) ,
                                                                                     ( <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/realizes>
                                                                                       <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/potentialOf>
                                                                                     ) ;
                                                              rdfs:comment "A property chain axiom secures that a participant in part of an activity participates in the activity as a whole." ;
                                                              rdfs:label "hasParticipant" ;
                                                              rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000057> ,
                                                                           <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000057> ,
                                                                           <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/participatesIn> ,
                                                                           "ISO 15926-2:2003 'participation'" ;
                                                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A pump participates in (a) pumping (activity), an electric transformer participates in voltage conversion, a stream of water participates in dilution, a bolt participates in a connection." ;
                                                              <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                              <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has participant' y, then x is an 'activity', and y is an 'object' that participates in x." ;
                                                              <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "The notion of participation is primitive." ;
                                                              <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "A property chain axiom secures that when a realizable (a 'disposition' or 'role') is 'realized in' an activity, the activity has the bearer as a participant." ,
                                                                                                                                                        "A property chain axiom secures that when an activity has a 'profile quantity datum', the bearer of the quantity is a participant in the activity." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasParticipant> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000057> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000057 is 'has participant at some time'."
 ] .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasParticipant> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000057> ;
   rdfs:comment "RO_0000057 is 'has participant'."
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasParticipantQualityQuantifiedAs
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasParticipantQualityQuantifiedAs> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                                 rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/representedIn> ;
                                                                                 owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/quantifiesQualityOfParticipantIn> ;
                                                                                 rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Activity> ;
                                                                                 rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/QualityDatum> ;
                                                                                 rdfs:label "hasParticipantQualityQuantifiedAs" ;
                                                                                 rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/quantifiesQualityOfParticipantIn> ;
                                                                                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Pressure of a stream during a pumping activity, the voltage provided to a motor during a test run." ;
                                                                                 <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                                 <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has participant quality quantified as' y, then x is an 'activity', y is a 'quality datum', and at a time within (inclusive) the duration of x, y 'quantifies quality' a 'quality' of a participant in x." ;
                                                                                 <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "The notion of \"during\" used here goes beyond OWL expressivity." ;
                                                                                 <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "Suitable as a superproperty for properties that assign aggregate datums to activities, to assign average, maximum, or minimum quantification datums." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPassiveParticipant
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPassiveParticipant> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                     rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasParticipant> ;
                                                                     owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/passiveParticipantIn> ;
                                                                     rdfs:label "hasPassiveParticipant" ;
                                                                     rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/passiveParticipantIn> ;
                                                                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A metal plate is perforated in a drilling activity, a volume of liquid is heated in a heat transmission activity, a loading ramp is the location of an offloading activity, a fluid medium is pumped, a piece of metal is shaped, a stream of data is filtered." ;
                                                                     <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                     <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "if x 'has passive participant' y, then x is a passive participant in y." ;
                                                                     <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "The distinction between active and participation participation is primitive." ;
                                                                     <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "This is a covering relation for passive participation, i.e., being acted on by other participants in an activity, or playing a supporting role." ,
                                                                                                                                                               "With OWL property chains, the right kind of participation can be secured for activities that count as realizations of 'potential' individuals. As in, a bolt is a passive participant in a bolt-driving activity, where its disposition to enter a threaded hole is realized (distinct from the bolt's function, which is realized in a subsequent activity of holding pieces together)." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPhysicalQuantity
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPhysicalQuantity> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                   rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasQuality> ;
                                                                   owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/physicalQuantityOf> ;
                                                                   rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/PhysicalObject> ;
                                                                   rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/PhysicalQuantity> ;
                                                                   rdfs:label "hasPhysicalQuantity" ;
                                                                   rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/physicalQuantityOf> ;
                                                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A section of pipe has length, a crane has lifting power, a flange has inner diameter." ;
                                                                   <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                   <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "x 'has physical quantity' y if and only if x 'has quality' y, and y is a 'physical quantity'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPotential
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPotential> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                            owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/potentialOf> ;
                                                            rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Object> ;
                                                            rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Potential> ;
                                                            rdfs:comment "Generic relation for assigning  'potential' entities (typically, dispositions or roles) to bearers." ;
                                                            rdfs:label "hasPotential" ;
                                                            rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000196> ,
                                                                         <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053> ,
                                                                         <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/potentialOf> ;
                                                            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Having a role, function, obligation, or plan (intention to act)." ;
                                                            <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "The pre-defined types of 'potential' entities in IDO are 'role', 'disposition', and 'interest'. If other kinds are needed for use case, then 'has potential' is a suitable superrelation for the corresponding bearer relations." ;
                                                            <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                            <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has potential' y, then x is an 'object', and y is a 'potential' that is dependent on x." ;
                                                            <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "The relation of dependence is not defined in IDO." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPotential> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000196> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000196 is 'bearer of', a more generic relation than 'has potential' in that its range is any 'specifically dependent continuant', which in IDO corresponds to 'dependent'."
 ] .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPotential> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000053> ;
   rdfs:comment "RO_0000053 is 'has characteristic', which in the Relation Ontology also has 'quality of' as a subrelation."
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPrimaryParticipant
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPrimaryParticipant> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                     rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasParticipant> ;
                                                                     owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/primaryParticipantIn> ;
                                                                     rdfs:label "hasPrimaryParticipant" ;
                                                                     rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/primaryParticipantIn> ;
                                                                     <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A pump is the performer in a pumping activity, a thermometer is the performer in a temperature measurement." ;
                                                                     <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                     <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has primary participant' y, then x is a realization of a disposition or role of y that is essential to the identification of x." ;
                                                                     <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "The notion of primary participant is not defined." ;
                                                                     <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "Assume p is a pump, a an activity that realizes the function fp of p, and no subactivity x of a realizes fp (except for subactivities determined solely by restriction to a temporal sub-interval). For instance, the subactivity of the motor that drives the impeller realizes a function of the motor, but this is not by itself a realization of the function of the pump as a whole, hence the motor is not a 'primary participant'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasQuality
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasQuality> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                          owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/qualityOf> ;
                                                          rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Object> ;
                                                          rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Quality> ;
                                                          rdfs:label "hasQuality" ;
                                                          rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000196> ,
                                                                       <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000086> ,
                                                                       <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/qualityOf> ;
                                                          <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A motor has rated output power, a lightbulb has luminance, an amount of liquid has mass, a bar of metal has chemical composition, a document has readability." ;
                                                          <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                          <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has quality' y, then x is an 'object', and y is a 'quality' that is dependent on x." ;
                                                          <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "The relation of dependence is not defined in IDO." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasQuality> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000196> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000196 is 'bearer of', a more generic relation than 'has quality' in that its range is any 'specifically dependent continuant', which in IDO corresponds to 'dependent'."
 ] .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasQuality> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000086> ;
   rdfs:comment "RO_0000086 is 'has quality' in the Relations Ontology."
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasQualityQuantifiedAs
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasQualityQuantifiedAs> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                      rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/representedIn> ;
                                                                      owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/quantifiesQualityOf> ;
                                                                      rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Object> ;
                                                                      rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/QualityDatum> ;
                                                                      owl:propertyChainAxiom ( <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasQuality>
                                                                                               <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/qualityQuantifiedAs>
                                                                                             ) ;
                                                                      rdfs:label "hasQualityQuantifiedAs" ;
                                                                      rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/quantifiesQualityOf> ;
                                                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The GeoSPARQL object property geo:hasLength relates (spatial) objects to datums that provide length with number and unit of measure. lis:hasQualityQuantifiedAs is suitable as a superproperty in an alignment with GeoSPARQL data that includes geo:hasLength relationships." ;
                                                                      <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                      <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has quality quantified as' y, then x is an 'object', and y is a 'quality datum' that 'quantifies quality' a 'quality' of x." ;
                                                                      <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "This is an informally \"abstract\" superproperty of \"shortcut\" relations that relate objects directly to quality datums, leaving the quality implicit." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasResident
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasResident> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                           rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/locatedRelativeTo> ;
                                                           owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/residesIn> ;
                                                           rdfs:label "hasResident" ;
                                                           rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/residesIn> ,
                                                                        "ISO 15926-2:2003 'relative_location'" ;
                                                           <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                           <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'resides in'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasRole
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasRole> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                       rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPotential> ;
                                                       owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/roleOf> ;
                                                       rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Role> ;
                                                       rdfs:comment "Inspired by BFO's \"has role\" (RO_0000087)" ;
                                                       rdfs:label "hasRole" ;
                                                       rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000087> ,
                                                                    <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/roleOf> ,
                                                                    "ISO 15926-2:2003 'role'" ;
                                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "An window has the role of a ventilation opening, a room has the role of a storage space, a gas sensor has the role of a leak detector, a person has the role of inspector." ;
                                                       <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                       <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "x 'has role' y if and only if x 'has potential' y, and y is a 'role'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasSpatialExtent
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasSpatialExtent> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/locatedRelativeTo> ;
                                                                owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/spatialExtentOf> ;
                                                                rdf:type owl:FunctionalProperty ;
                                                                rdfs:domain [ rdf:type owl:Class ;
                                                                              owl:unionOf ( <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/PhysicalObject>
                                                                                            <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Site>
                                                                                          )
                                                                            ] ;
                                                                rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/SpatialLocation> ;
                                                                rdfs:label "hasSpatialExtent" ;
                                                                rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000210> ,
                                                                             <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/spatialExtentOf> ,
                                                                             <http://www.loa-cnr.it/ontologies/DOLCE-Lite.owl#exact-location> ;
                                                                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The volume occupied by an process skid, the volume occupied by a volume of flammable gas." ;
                                                                <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has spatial extent' y, then x is a 'physical object', and y is the 'spatial location' determined as the extension in space of x." ;
                                                                <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "The notion of  \"spatial extension\" of an object is not fully defined." ;
                                                                <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "The 'site' of an object will occupy different 'spatial location's over time if the location and size of the object changes." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasSpatialExtent> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000210> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000210 is 'occupies spatial region at some time' (from BFO-ISO)"
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasSpatiotemporalExtent
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasSpatiotemporalExtent> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                       rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/occursRelativeTo> ;
                                                                       owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/spatiotemporalExtentOf> ;
                                                                       rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Activity> ;
                                                                       rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/SpatiotemporalRegion> ;
                                                                       rdfs:label "hasSpatiotemporalExtent" ;
                                                                       rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000200> ,
                                                                                    "lis:" ;
                                                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A pipeline pig occupies the spatiotemporal region which is its trajectory (adopted from BFO-ISO)." ;
                                                                       <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                       <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has spatiotemporal extent' y, then x is an activity, and y is a spatiotemporal region which is the spatiotemporal extent of x." ;
                                                                       <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "The notion of spatiotemporal extension is primitive." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasSpatiotemporalExtent> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000200> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000200 is 'occupies spatiotemporal region'."
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasSubLocation
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasSubLocation> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                              rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPart> ,
                                                                                 <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/locatedRelativeTo> ;
                                                              owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/subLocationOf> ;
                                                              rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Location> ;
                                                              rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Location> ;
                                                              rdfs:label "hasSubLocation" ;
                                                              rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/subLocationOf> ;
                                                              <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The landing area is a sublocation of the helicopter deck." ;
                                                              <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                              <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has sublocation' y, then x and y are locations, and x 'has part' y." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasTemporalExtent
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasTemporalExtent> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                 rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/occursRelativeTo> ;
                                                                 owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/temporalExtentOf> ;
                                                                 rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Temporal> ;
                                                                 rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/TemporalRegion> ;
                                                                 rdfs:label "hasTemporalExtent" ;
                                                                 rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000199> ,
                                                                              <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/temporalExtentOf> ;
                                                                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A well drilling activity takes place in a 20-hour interval, a control system is switched on at 10:00." ;
                                                                 <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                 <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has temporal extent' y, then x is a 'temporal' entity, and y is a temporal region which is the temporal extent of x." ;
                                                                 <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "The notion of temporal extension is primitive." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasTemporalExtent> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000199> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000199 is 'occupies temporal region'."
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasTemporalPart
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasTemporalPart> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                               rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPart> ;
                                                               owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/temporalPartOf> ;
                                                               rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Temporal> ;
                                                               rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Temporal> ;
                                                               rdfs:label "hasTemporalPart" ;
                                                               rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/temporalPartOf> ;
                                                               <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A specific day is a temporal part of a specific week." ;
                                                               <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                               <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'has temporal part' y, then x and y are temporal entities, and y is a part of x." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/implementedBy
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/implementedBy> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                             owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/implements> ;
                                                             rdfs:label "implementedBy" ;
                                                             rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/implements> ;
                                                             <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                             <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'implements'" .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/implements
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/implements> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                          rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Actual> ;
                                                          rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Specified> ;
                                                          rdfs:label "implements" ;
                                                          rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/implementedBy> ;
                                                          <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Pump P-101 is a tag, and ACME pumps with serial numbers 457636 and 457711 implement (have been installed as) this pump." ;
                                                          <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "The 'implements' relation is central to the intended use of IDO. It allows for a record of different individuals being installed or otherwise serving as a specified object over time. Typically, a serial-numbered artefact is installed as a \"specification\" individual (a \"tag\") at one time, and later replaced with another serial-numbered artefact. The 'implements' relation carries semantic restrictions only to ensure no object is both Actual and Specified. No further constraints are given, to allow 'implements' relationships even where restrictions on the specification object are inconsistent with those on the implementing (installed) object." ;
                                                          <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/explanatoryNote> "The domain and range restrictions to disjunct classes 'actual' and 'specified' prevent chains of 'implements' relationships." ;
                                                          <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                          <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'implements' y, then x is a 'specified' entity, y is an 'actual' entity, and at some time, x is the same individual as y." ;
                                                          <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "'implements' is used to express identity relationships that may vary over time. Because OWL lacks time indices, the representation is informal." ;
                                                          <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "An asset model with 'implements' relationships supports compatibility checks for implementing objects, to uncover possible violations of requirements.  This is requires a transformation of the asset model, as follows: replace each 'implements'/'implementedBy' relationship with identity (owl:sameAs), and replace classifications as 'specified' or 'actual' with just 'object' for the participant individuals.  Any semantic inconsistency between the the specified object and the implementing object may then be discovered by OWL reasoning." ,
                                                                                                                                                    "Periods of 'implements' relationships should be recorded using OWL annotations, to enable prescriptive objects to be matched with installed objects for selected points or periods in time. A detailed representation using 'role' is also possible." ,
                                                                                                                                                    "The mechanism for checking requirement consistency on 'implements' relationships must be implemented as a transformation that is external to the OWL ontology." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/interestOf
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/interestOf> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                          rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/potentialOf> ;
                                                          rdfs:label "interestOf" ;
                                                          rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasInterest> ;
                                                          <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                          <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'has interest'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/isAbout
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/isAbout> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                       owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/representedIn> ;
                                                       rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/InformationObject> ;
                                                       rdfs:label "isAbout" ;
                                                       rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000136> ,
                                                                    <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/representedIn> ,
                                                                    "ISO 15926-2:2003 'representation_of_thing'" ;
                                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A regulation describes a procedure, a datum quantifies a quality, a nameplate provides basic information about a pressure vessel, a log file traces quantity values during an activity." ;
                                                       <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "The 'is about' relation is intended as a superrelation for the broad range of relations between information objects and entities, including describing, naming, characterisation, and evaluation." ;
                                                       <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                       <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'is about' y, then x is an 'information object' of relevance to y." ;
                                                       <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "A comprehensive account of aboutness is beyond the scope of IDO." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/isAbout> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000136> ;
   rdfs:comment "IAO_0000136 is 'is about', in the Information Artifact Ontology."
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/locatedRelativeTo
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/locatedRelativeTo> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ,
                                                                          owl:SymmetricProperty ;
                                                                 rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Object> ;
                                                                 rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Object> ;
                                                                 rdfs:label "locatedRelativeTo" ;
                                                                 rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000171> ,
                                                                              <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000210> ,
                                                                              <http://www.loa-cnr.it/ontologies/DOLCE-Lite.owl#generic-location> ,
                                                                              "ISO 15926-2:2003 'relative_location'" ;
                                                                 <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "An outlet is below an inlet, a door is inside an opening, a motor is inside an enclosure." ;
                                                                 <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                 <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x is 'located relative to' y, then x and y are 'object's with location in space." ;
                                                                 <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "The notion of relative location in space is introduced with this relation." ;
                                                                 <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "This relation is \"abstract\" (in the object-orientation sense of the word) in that it serves only as a parent relation to specialized relations of relative location." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/locatedRelativeTo> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000171> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000171 is 'located in at some time' in BFO-ISO. This relation has domain and range restricted to 'independent continuant' and not 'spatial region', meaning it's a relation between entities that are material objects or determined by material objects, only."
 ] .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/locatedRelativeTo> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000210> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000210 is 'occupies spatial region at some time' in BFO-ISO. This relation has domain restricted to 'independent continuant' and not 'spatial region', and range to 'spatial region', meaning it's a relation from entities that are material objects or determined by material objects, to spatial regions determined independently of material objects."
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/materialPartOf
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/materialPartOf> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                              rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/partOf> ;
                                                              rdfs:label "materialPartOf" ;
                                                              rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasMaterialPart> ;
                                                              <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                              <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'has material part'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/occursIn
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/occursIn> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                        owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/siteOf> ;
                                                        rdfs:label "occursIn" ;
                                                        rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000066> ,
                                                                     <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/siteOf> ;
                                                        <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                        <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'site of'." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/occursIn> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000066> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000066 is 'occurs in'"
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/occursRelativeTo
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/occursRelativeTo> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ,
                                                                         owl:SymmetricProperty ;
                                                                rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Temporal> ;
                                                                rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Temporal> ;
                                                                rdfs:comment "This relation is introduced for the DL profile as a top relation for various temporal relations between activities (only)." ;
                                                                rdfs:label "occursRelativeTo" ;
                                                                rdfs:seeAlso "ISO 15926-2:2003 'temporal_sequence'" ;
                                                                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A vessel is emptied before inspection, a valve is opened before draining of a pipeline, firmware is installed before the equipment begins to operate." ;
                                                                <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'occurs relative to' y, then x and y are 'temporal' entities, with temporal location." ;
                                                                <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "The notion of relative location in time is introduced with this relation." ;
                                                                <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "This relation is \"abstract\" (in the object-orientation sense of the word) in that it serves only as a parent relation to specialised relations of relative temporal location." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/partOf
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/partOf> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                      rdfs:label "partOf" ;
                                                      rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPart> ;
                                                      <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                      <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'has part'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/participantIn
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/participantIn> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                             rdfs:label "participantIn" ;
                                                             rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasParticipant> ;
                                                             <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                             <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'has participant'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/passiveParticipantIn
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/passiveParticipantIn> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                    rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/participantIn> ;
                                                                    rdfs:label "passiveParticipantIn" ;
                                                                    rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPassiveParticipant> ;
                                                                    <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                    <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'has passive participant'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/physicalQuantityOf
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/physicalQuantityOf> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                  rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/qualityOf> ;
                                                                  rdfs:label "physicalQuantityOf" ;
                                                                  rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPhysicalQuantity> ;
                                                                  <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                  <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'has physical quantity'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/potentialOf
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/potentialOf> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                           rdfs:comment "Generic relation from a 'potential' to the bearer (or, for the less common cases of multiply dependent realizable entities, to the bearers)." ,
                                                                        "This relation is used in the property chain for 'has participant', for inferring participation in a temporal entity (typically, an activity)." ;
                                                           rdfs:label "potentialOf" ;
                                                           rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPotential> ;
                                                           <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                           <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'has potential'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/primaryParticipantIn
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/primaryParticipantIn> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                    rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/participantIn> ;
                                                                    rdfs:label "primaryParticipantIn" ;
                                                                    rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasPrimaryParticipant> ;
                                                                    <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                    <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'has primary participant'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/profileOfQuality
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/profileOfQuality> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/qualityProfiledIn> ;
                                                                rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/ActivityProfile> ;
                                                                rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Quality> ;
                                                                owl:propertyChainAxiom ( <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/profileQuantityDatum>
                                                                                         <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/quantifiesQuality>
                                                                                       ) ;
                                                                rdfs:label "profileOfQuality" ;
                                                                rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/qualityProfiledIn> ;
                                                                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A temperature activity profile of a heating process represents just that part of the process which is a variation in temperature." ;
                                                                <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote> "'profile of quality' should be considered a functional property (i.e., an 'activity profile' is a profile of only a single 'quality'). However, in OWL, an object property with property chain restrictions may not be combined with cardinality restrictions. Correct cardinalities must therefore be maintained with rules external to the ontology." ;
                                                                <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "x is a 'profile of quality' y if and only if x is an 'activity profile' that varies only in the 'quality' y." ;
                                                                <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "A property chain axiom ensures that a quantity datum individual associated with an activity profile by 'profile quantity datum' quantifies a quality which defines the activity profile by 'profile of quality'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/profileQuantityDatum
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/profileQuantityDatum> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                    rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasParticipantQualityQuantifiedAs> ;
                                                                    owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/quantityDatumOfProfile> ;
                                                                    rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/ActivityProfile> ;
                                                                    rdfs:comment "Intuitively, 'profile quantity datum' should only point to quantity data recorded while the activity is taking place. This can not be enforced with OWL restrictions on the relation (it would require a \"diamond\" pattern). However, with a suitable date or time data property value restriction, an individual activity can constrain related quantity data." ;
                                                                    rdfs:label "profileQuantityDatum" ;
                                                                    rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/quantityDatumOfProfile> ;
                                                                    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The pressure of a liquid is measured at 10, 11, and 12 bar at different points of time during a transport activity." ;
                                                                    <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                    <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x has 'profile quantity datum' y, then x is an 'activity profile', and x 'has participant quality quantified as' y." ;
                                                                    <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "Assume y is an 'activity profile', obtained from some containing activity z by selective abstraction on a quality q of a participant in z. Then, relate y by 'profile quantity datum' to magnitudes of q that are recorded during the execution of y." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/qualityOf
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/qualityOf> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                         rdfs:label "qualityOf" ;
                                                         rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasQuality> ;
                                                         <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                         <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'has quality'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/qualityProfiledIn
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/qualityProfiledIn> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                 rdfs:label "qualityProfiledIn" ;
                                                                 rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/profileOfQuality> ;
                                                                 <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                 <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'profile of quality'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/qualityQuantifiedAs
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/qualityQuantifiedAs> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                   rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/representedIn> ;
                                                                   owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/quantifiesQuality> ;
                                                                   rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Quality> ;
                                                                   rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/QualityDatum> ;
                                                                   rdfs:label "qualityQuantifiedAs" ;
                                                                   rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000417> ,
                                                                                <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/quantifiesQuality> ,
                                                                                <http://www.w3.org/ns/ssn/observedProperty> ,
                                                                                "ISO 15926-2:2003 'property_quantification'" ;
                                                                   <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "The nominal outer diameter of a pipe is 324 mm, the measured temperature of a boiler is 150 degrees Celsius, the colour of a surface is 'red'." ;
                                                                   <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                   <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x is a 'quality quantified as' y, then x is an 'quality' that is 'represented in' the 'quality datum' y." ;
                                                                   <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "The range of 'quality quantified as' is 'quality datum', which includes data that don't follow the \"unit of measure with value\" pattern. Examples are colours and chemical composition categories." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/qualityQuantifiedAs> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000417> ;
   rdfs:comment "IAO_0000417 is 'is quality measured as' of the Information Artefact Ontology. In IDO, the term \"quantified\" replaces \"measured\" to support cases where measurement is not involved, as in, e.g., estimates."
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/quantifiesQuality
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/quantifiesQuality> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                 rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/isAbout> ;
                                                                 rdfs:label "quantifiesQuality" ;
                                                                 rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/qualityQuantifiedAs> ;
                                                                 <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                 <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'quality quantified as'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/quantifiesQualityOf
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/quantifiesQualityOf> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                   rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/isAbout> ;
                                                                   rdfs:label "quantifiesQualityOf" ;
                                                                   rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasQualityQuantifiedAs> ;
                                                                   <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                   <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'has quality quantified as'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/quantifiesQualityOfParticipantIn
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/quantifiesQualityOfParticipantIn> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                                rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/isAbout> ;
                                                                                rdfs:label "quantifiesQualityOfParticipantIn" ;
                                                                                rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasParticipantQualityQuantifiedAs> ;
                                                                                <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                                <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'has participant quality quantified as'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/quantityDatumOfProfile
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/quantityDatumOfProfile> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                                      rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/quantifiesQualityOfParticipantIn> ;
                                                                      rdfs:label "quantityDatumOfProfile" ;
                                                                      rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/profileQuantityDatum> ;
                                                                      <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                                      <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'profile quantity datum'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/realizedIn
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/realizedIn> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                          owl:inverseOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/realizes> ;
                                                          rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Potential> ;
                                                          rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Activity> ;
                                                          rdfs:label "realizedIn" ;
                                                          rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054> ,
                                                                       <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/realizes> ;
                                                          <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "A pump realizes its function in a pumping (activity), a bolt realizes its function in a connection, a software monitoring application realizes its function in streaming sensor data." ;
                                                          <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                          <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x is 'realized in' y, then x is a 'potential', and y is an 'activity' that successfully realizes x." ;
                                                          <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "A full account of the notion of \"successfully realizes\" is beyond the scope of IDO. It depends on an account of \"success\", in that failed activities will not be realizations, and on the bearer of the potential participating in the realizing activity in the right way." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/realizedIn> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000054> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000054 is 'has realization' in BFO-ISO, and 'realized in' in the Relations Ontology."
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/realizes
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/realizes> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                        rdfs:label "realizes" ;
                                                        rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000055> ,
                                                                     <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/realizedIn> ;
                                                        <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                        <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'realized in'." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/realizes> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000055> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000055 is 'realizes' in BFO-ISO."
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/representedIn
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/representedIn> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                             rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/InformationObject> ;
                                                             rdfs:label "representedIn" ;
                                                             rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/isAbout> ;
                                                             <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                             <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'is about'." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/residesIn
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/residesIn> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                         rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/locatedRelativeTo> ;
                                                         rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/PhysicalObject> ;
                                                         rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Location> ;
                                                         rdfs:label "residesIn" ;
                                                         rdfs:seeAlso <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasResident> ,
                                                                      "ISO 15926-2:2003 'relative_location'" ;
                                                         <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "An engine is located in a machine room, a pressure vessel is located in an outdoors plant area." ;
                                                         <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                         <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'resides in' y, then x is a 'physical object', y is a 'location', and x is located entirely within y." ;
                                                         <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "The notion of being \"located within\" is not fully defined here, leaving open whether this is understood in terms of boundaries of physical objects or a fixed frame of reference." ;
                                                         <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "This relation may be used where an object x is located in a site y, defined in terms of boundaries of a physical object, that may change its location over time." .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/roleOf
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/roleOf> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                      rdfs:subPropertyOf <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/potentialOf> ;
                                                      rdfs:label "roleOf" ;
                                                      rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000081> ,
                                                                   <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/hasRole> ,
                                                                   "ISO 15926-2:2003 'role'" ;
                                                      <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "false"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                      <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/usageNote> "For annotations, see the inverse relation 'has role'." .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/roleOf> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/RO_0000081> ;
   rdfs:comment "RO_0000081 is 'role of' in the Relations Ontology."
 ] .


###  http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/siteOf
<http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/siteOf> rdf:type owl:ObjectProperty ;
                                                      rdfs:domain <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Site> ;
                                                      rdfs:range <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/Activity> ;
                                                      rdfs:label "siteOf" ;
                                                      rdfs:seeAlso <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000067> ,
                                                                   <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000183> ,
                                                                   <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000217> ,
                                                                   <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/occursIn> ;
                                                      <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example> "Mixing takes place within a vessel, transport takes place in a pipeline" ;
                                                      <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/isPrimitive> "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
                                                      <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/naturalLanguageDefinition> "If x 'site of' y, then x is a 'site', y is an 'activity', and y takes place entirely within x." ;
                                                      <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/primitiveRationale> "x 'site of' y means, the spatial extent of the site contains the spatial extent of the activity for the duration of the activity. This requires a relation of \"spatial projection throughout the time of the activity\", which is not included in IDO. (The BFO-ISO definition expresses this using the temporalized relation 'spatially projects onto at all times'.)" ;
                                                      <https://spec.industrialontologies.org/ontology/core/meta/AnnotationVocabulary/synonym> "environs" .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/siteOf> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000067> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000067 is 'contains process', from RO, where an annotation says the 'editor preferred term' is \"site of\". There are subtle differences in the range and domain restrictions between BFO's 'environs' and RO's 'contains process': where RO has domain as the broad 'independent continuant' only, BFO has ('site' or 'material entity'); where RO has range as 'occurrent', BFO has ('process' or 'process boundary')."
 ] .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/siteOf> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000183> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000183 is 'environs' from BFO"
 ] .

[ rdf:type owl:Axiom ;
   owl:annotatedSource <http://rds.posccaesar.org/ontology/lis14/rdl/siteOf> ;
   owl:annotatedProperty rdfs:seeAlso ;
   owl:annotatedTarget <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/BFO_0000217> ;
   rdfs:comment "BFO_0000217 is 'spatially projects onto at all times'."
 ] .


